=begin
      author: Fizzleworth, Ashraam
        name: reanim
        game: gemstone
        tags: necromancer, reanimate, animate dead, combat
    requires: Lich > 5.14.2
     version: 0.4
        note: Written with assistance from Claude (Anthropic).

  Kills a target with repeated Pain (711), then reanimates the corpse with
  Animate Dead (730) and sets the new animate to work.

  Can be run two ways:
    - From Bigshot, passing an explicit target: ;reanim <#targetid>
    - Manually during a hunt: ;reanim
      Target resolution order: an explicit #id you passed, then your formal
      /target lock (GameObj.target) if you have one, then the first living
      NPC in the room. Your own minor demon (matched via IGNORE_NPCS,
      currently "verlok") is never picked as a target. If nothing resolves,
      the room is considered empty and the script does nothing.

  Sequence:
    1) Cast Pain (711) on the target repeatedly (up to MAX_PAIN_ATTEMPTS
       times) until it's dead or gone.
    2) Appraise the corpse (logged under DEBUG) -- suitability wording is
       informational only, not a gate; reanimation is attempted either way.
       This step never fires until the target's status is confirmed
       dead/gone (with a short pause after the last Pain cast to avoid
       reading a stale pre-death status), so it won't appraise a live NPC.
    3) Prep and cast Animate Dead (730) on the corpse.
    4) "tell anim follow", "tell anim attack", then arm it:
       a) make sure a spare <WEAPON> is on the ground -- tell verlok (your
          minor demon) to drop one (skipped if one's already lying here).
       b) "tell anim to get <WEAPON>", looping until it's actually off the
          ground. If the animate won't take it because its hands are full
          with two other weapons, drop the off-hand junk and retry.
       c) once it has the <WEAPON> (animates auto-wield the better weapon),
          "tell anim to drop" everything else it's still holding -- its
          innate whip, an old spare. These only drop once they're NOT the
          wielded weapon, which is why this is done AFTER the pickup, not
          before. (The bare "tell anim drop <x>" form fails with "I could
          not find what you were referring to." -- must be "tell anim TO
          drop <x>". Observed 2026-09-08.)

  reanim_weapon (UserVar, default "katana") is what the animate should wield.
  Use the item's BASE noun -- the last word of its inventory name ("massive
  bone-hilted claidhmore" -> "claidhmore", "well-balanced gornar halberd" ->
  "halberd"). A shorter targeting noun ("claid") is matched too, but the base
  noun is an exact match for what LOOK reports it holding.
    ;vars set reanim_weapon=claidhmore
  The minor demon must be set to follow ("tell mdem to follow" -- Fizzleworth-
  prep does this) so it's in the room to drop the spare.

  Both 711 and 730 are cast via Spell#cast, which queues through Lich's
  shared cast lock instead of raw release/incant fput -- the same fix
  applied to fizzsac.lic to avoid racing Bigshot's own spell casts.

  Set DEBUG = true/false at the top of the script to toggle status messages.

  Usage:  ;reanim              kill + reanimate + arm one target
          ;reanim #<id>        same, explicit target (bigshot passes this)
          ;reanim die          end-of-hunt teardown: wait for the animate to
                               catch up (it's on follow), get the spare
                               weapon back onto verlok, "tell anim die",
                               then ;eloot the collapsed animate for the
                               original creature's treasure -- so we don't
                               drag an animated corpse (or lose the weapon
                               / leave the loot) when we
                               head to town. No-op if no animate is up.
                               Fired early (in the field) by
                               Fizzleworth-anim-cleanup.lic, with
                               Fizzleworth-prerest as a town fallback.
  Stop:   n/a (single pass, exits when done)
=end

DEBUG = true

IGNORE_NPCS = /verlok|animated/i   # your own minor demon / an existing animate -- never a valid target

PAIN_SPELL          = 711
ANIMATE_SPELL       = 730
MAX_PAIN_ATTEMPTS   = 15
WEAPON_PICKUP_TRIES = 4
ANIMATE_CATCHUP     = 10   # ;reanim die: secs to wait for the animate to follow in

# Set true when Animate Dead lands, false once ;reanim die has torn the buddy
# down. `Spell[730].active?` stays true for the spell's whole duration even
# after "tell anim die", so it's useless as a "do we still have a buddy?"
# check -- this global is the source of truth. Survives across ;reanim runs.
$reanim_animate_live = false unless defined?($reanim_animate_live)

# The weapon the animate should wield.  Use the item's BASE noun -- the last
# word of how it shows in inventory ("massive bone-hilted claidhmore" -> set
# "claidhmore"; "well-balanced gornar halberd" -> "halberd").  A shorter
# targeting noun ("claid") also works, but the base noun is an exact match for
# what LOOK reports the animate holding.   ;vars set reanim_weapon=claidhmore
UserVars.reanim_weapon = "katana" if UserVars.reanim_weapon.to_s.strip.empty?
WEAPON = UserVars.reanim_weapon.to_s.strip

def debug(msg)
	echo "[DBG] #{msg}" if DEBUG
end

# Do two weapon nouns refer to the same weapon? `reanim_weapon` is a game
# TARGETING noun ("claid"), while a LOOK / GameObj.loot name gives the
# descriptive last word ("claidhmore"). Treat either being a prefix of the
# other as a match -- "claid" <-> "claidhmore", "halberd" <-> "halberd".
def same_weapon?(a, b)
	a = a.to_s.downcase.strip
	b = b.to_s.downcase.strip
	return false if a.empty? || b.empty?
	a == b || a.start_with?(b) || b.start_with?(a)
end

# Is a weapon matching `noun` lying on the ground? Match `noun` against each
# word of every loot item's name (so "claid" finds "massive bone-hilted
# claidhmore") -- NOT a /\bnoun\b/ regex, which fails when the item's real
# name extends the noun ("claid" + "hmore").
def weapon_on_ground(noun)
	GameObj.loot.find do |o|
		o && o.name.to_s.split(/\s+/).any? { |w| same_weapon?(w, noun) }
	end
end

# LOOK at the animate (by id, so it can't match a live mob of the same type)
# and return the noun(s) of what it's HELDING, dropping "(worn)" items. GS4
# phrases this as:
#   "He has a green leather whip and a pair of tight leather armbands (worn)."
# -> ["whip"].  [] = confirmed empty-handed.  nil = LOOK couldn't be parsed.
def animate_held_nouns
	mine = GameObj.npcs.find { |n| n && n.name.to_s =~ /\banimate/i }
	tgt  = mine ? "##{mine.id}" : "animate"
	lines = Lich::Util.issue_command("look #{tgt}",
	          /\b(?:has|have)\b|empty[- ]handed|hands? (?:are|is) empty|nothing in (?:its|his|her|their)/i,
	          include_end: false, silent: true) rescue []
	return [] if lines.any? { |l| l =~ /empty[- ]handed|hands? (?:are|is) empty|nothing in (?:its|his|her|their)/i }

	line = lines.find { |l| l =~ /\b(?:has|have)\s+(?:a|an|some|two|three|four|several|a pair of)\b/i &&
	                        l !~ /good shape|appears to be|wound|scar|bruis|blood|injur|gash|slice/i }
	return nil unless line

	m = line.match(/\b(?:has|have)\s+(.+?)\.?\s*$/i)
	return nil unless m
	m[1].split(/\s*,\s*|\s+and\s+/i)
	    .reject { |item| item =~ /\(worn\)/i }
	    .map    { |item| item.sub(/\s*\([^)]*\)\s*$/, "").strip.split(/\s+/).last.to_s.downcase }
	    .reject(&:empty?)
	    .uniq
rescue StandardError
	nil
end

# Tell the animate to drop every weapon it's holding EXCEPT `keep` (the one we
# want it wielding). Uses "tell anim TO drop <noun>" -- the bare "tell anim
# drop <noun>" form fails with "I could not find what you were referring to."
# (observed 2026-09-08). No-op if the LOOK can't be parsed (better to leave a
# stray whip in the off-hand than guess at nouns).
# NOTE: an animate can't drop the weapon it's actively WIELDING, so this only
# succeeds on off-hand items -- call it AFTER the animate has picked up `keep`
# and switched to it. The switch can lag a round or two, so retry once on the
# "could not find" (= still wielded) response.
DROP_OK  = /drops (?:a|an|the)|not (?:holding|carrying)|isn't (?:holding|carrying)|empty[- ]handed/i
DROP_NOT = /could not find|not able to make out/i
def drop_other_weapons(keep)
	held = animate_held_nouns
	return false if held.nil?
	dropped_any = false
	held.reject { |w| same_weapon?(w, keep) }.each do |w|
		2.times do |t|
			r = dothistimeout("tell anim to drop #{w}", 3, Regexp.union(DROP_OK, DROP_NOT)).to_s
			if r =~ DROP_OK || r !~ DROP_NOT
				dropped_any = true
				break
			end
			sleep 2   # still its wielded weapon -- give it a beat to switch to `keep`
		end
	end
	dropped_any
end

# Arm the animate with WEAPON:
#   1) make sure a WEAPON is on the ground (verlok drops one)
#   2) "tell anim to get WEAPON", looping until it's actually off the ground.
#      If it won't pick up (hands full with two other weapons), drop the
#      off-hand junk and retry.
#   3) once it has WEAPON (and auto-wields it -- animates take the better
#      weapon), drop whatever else it's still holding (its innate whip, an
#      old spare) -- droppable now that it's not the wielded weapon.
def verlok_here?
	GameObj.npcs.any? { |n| n && n.name.to_s =~ /verlok'?asha|minor demon/i }
rescue StandardError
	false
end

def arm_animate(noun)
	held = animate_held_nouns
	if held && held.any? { |w| same_weapon?(w, noun) }
		debug("animate already has a #{noun}")
		drop_other_weapons(noun)         # still clear the whip / old spare
		return
	end

	# 1) get a spare WEAPON onto the ground
	unless weapon_on_ground(noun)
		unless verlok_here?
			echo "[reanim] verlok isn't here -- nudging it to follow. ('tell mdem to follow' before a hunt.)"
			fput "tell mdem to follow"
			sleep 1
		end
		dothistimeout("tell verlok to drop #{noun}", 3,
			/drops (?:a|an|the)|could not find|isn't holding|not holding|does(?:n't| not) have|not here/i)
		# GameObj.loot can lag the drop line by a beat -- give it a moment
		15.times { break if weapon_on_ground(noun); sleep 0.2 }
		unless weapon_on_ground(noun)
			echo "[reanim] no #{noun} on the ground for the animate (verlok didn't drop one) -- animate left unarmed."
			return
		end
	end

	# 2) a spare IS on the ground now -- get the animate to take it
	picked = false
	WEAPON_PICKUP_TRIES.times do |i|
		gr = dothistimeout("tell anim to get #{noun}", 4,
			/snatches up|picks up|retriev|reaches down|takes hold of|obeys|obliges|hands full|cannot|can't|refuses/i)
		waitrt?
		sleep 1
		if weapon_on_ground(noun).nil?
			picked = true
			break
		end
		debug("#{noun} still on the ground after try #{i + 1}: get=#{gr.inspect}")
		drop_other_weapons(noun)         # hands full? clear the off-hand and retry
	end

	# 3) it has the WEAPON (auto-wields it) -- drop the innate whip / old spare
	if picked
		debug("animate has the #{noun}")
		drop_other_weapons(noun)
	else
		echo "[reanim] WARNING: animate wouldn't pick up the #{noun} -- check it."
	end
end

# Is there an animate IN THE CURRENT ROOM right now?
def animate_here?
	GameObj.npcs.any? { |n| n && n.name.to_s =~ /\banimate/i }
rescue StandardError
	false
end

# End-of-hunt teardown. Gated on $reanim_animate_live so it runs exactly once
# per hunt (Fizzleworth-anim-cleanup fires it in the field; Fizzleworth-prerest
# fires it again in town, where this is now an instant no-op). The caller
# freezes go2 / bigshot / sac4mana first; the animate is on "follow", so if
# travel already started it may be a room back -- wait for it, then get the
# spare WEAPON back onto verlok, dismiss it, and loot the remains.
def dismiss_animate(noun)
	unless $reanim_animate_live
		debug("no animate raised this hunt (or already torn down) -- nothing to do")
		return
	end

	waited = 0.0
	until animate_here? || waited >= ANIMATE_CATCHUP
		sleep 0.5
		waited += 0.5
	end
	here = animate_here?
	echo "[reanim] animate never reached the room -- dismissing it blind." unless here

	# 1) ask it to drop the spare (the "to" form -- bare "tell anim drop" fails;
	#    step 3 is the backstop -- a dying animate drops what it holds). Skip if
	#    it's not here.
	if here
		dothistimeout("tell anim to drop #{noun}", 3,
			/drops (?:a|an|the)|not (?:holding|carrying)|isn't (?:holding|carrying)|could not find|empty[- ]handed/i)
		sleep 0.4
	end

	# 2) dismiss it
	fput "tell anim die"
	sleep 1.5
	$reanim_animate_live = false
	echo "[reanim] animate still present after 'tell anim die' -- check it." if animate_here?

	return unless here   # nothing on the ground to reclaim / loot elsewhere

	# 3) whatever's on the ground now (the spare it dropped or died holding) ->
	#    back onto verlok so it isn't lost. If verlok won't, pick it up
	#    ourselves; ;eloot below is the final catch-all (into the pack).
	if weapon_on_ground(noun)
		dothistimeout("tell verlok to get #{noun}", 3,
			/picks up|snatches|grasps|retriev|reaches down|takes hold of|obeys|obliges|could not find|can't|cannot|refuses/i)
		sleep 0.4
		if weapon_on_ground(noun)
			dothistimeout("get #{noun}", 3, /You (?:pick up|get)|already have|What were you/i)
			sleep 0.3
			dothistimeout("give #{noun} to verlok", 3, /grudgingly accepts|hand(?:s)? .* to (?:a|an|the)|refuses|isn't interested/i)
			sleep 0.3
		end
	end

	# 4) loot the collapsed animate for the original creature's treasure
	#    (bigshot's own loot pass skipped it -- it was still "the animate").
	#    Run eloot detached with a hard cap: if it pauses itself for user input
	#    (sacks full, box handling) we must NOT stay blocked here -- the caller
	#    has bigshot / go2 / sac4mana frozen. Leave a paused eloot for the user.
	Script.start("eloot")
	deadline = Time.now + 15
	sleep 0.3 until !Script.running?("eloot") || Script.paused?("eloot") || Time.now > deadline
	echo "[reanim] eloot is still busy -- leaving it to finish on its own." if Script.running?("eloot")
end

args = script.vars[1..-1].to_a.compact.map(&:to_s).reject(&:empty?)

# ;reanim die  /  ;reanim --dismiss  -- end-of-hunt teardown, no killing.
# Wire it into bigshot's resting_commands (Fizzleworth-prerest) so the animate
# and its weapon don't come to town with us.
if args.any? { |a| a =~ /\A-{0,2}(?:die|dismiss|cleanup|teardown)\z/i }
	dismiss_animate(WEAPON)
	# Fizzleworth-attack-ultima reanims only the first inciter per hunt; this
	# teardown marks the hunt's end, so re-arm it for the next one.
	$ult_reanim_done = false
	exit
end

explicit_target = args.find { |a| a.start_with?("#") }

if explicit_target
	target = explicit_target
elsif GameObj.target and GameObj.target.name !~ IGNORE_NPCS
	target = "##{GameObj.target.id}"
else
	npc = GameObj.npcs.find { |n| n.status !~ /dead|gone/i and n.name !~ IGNORE_NPCS }
	target = npc ? "##{npc.id}" : nil
end

if target.nil?
	debug("Not doing anything because room is empty")
else
	search = target.delete_prefix("#")

	MAX_PAIN_ATTEMPTS.times do |attempt|
		find = GameObj.npcs.find { |n| n.id == search }
		break if find.nil? or find.status =~ /dead|gone/

		unless Spell[PAIN_SPELL].affordable?
			debug("Not enough resources to cast #{PAIN_SPELL}, stopping.")
			break
		end

		waitrt?
		waitcastrt?
		result = Spell[PAIN_SPELL].cast("##{find.id}")
		debug("Attempt #{attempt + 1}/#{MAX_PAIN_ATTEMPTS}: cast #{PAIN_SPELL} on ##{find.id} -> #{result}")
	end

	waitrt?
	sleep 0.5
	find = GameObj.npcs.find { |n| n.id == search }

	if find.nil?
		debug("Target is gone, nothing to reanimate.")
	elsif find.status !~ /dead|gone/
		debug("Target still alive after #{MAX_PAIN_ATTEMPTS} attempts, giving up.")
	else
		status = Lich::Util.issue_command("appraise ##{find.id}", /suitable for animation/i, include_end: false, silent: true).last
		debug("Appraise ##{find.id}: #{status}")

		unless Spell[ANIMATE_SPELL].affordable?
			debug("Not enough resources to cast #{ANIMATE_SPELL}.")
			exit
		end

		waitrt?
		waitcastrt?
		result = Spell[ANIMATE_SPELL].cast("##{find.id}")
		debug("Cast #{ANIMATE_SPELL} on ##{find.id} -> #{result}")
		$reanim_animate_live = true   # a buddy exists -> ;reanim die should tear it down

		waitrt?
		waitcastrt?
		fput "tell anim follow"
		sleep 0.3
		fput "tell anim attack"
		sleep 0.3
		arm_animate(WEAPON)
	end
end
